EXPERIMENT-3 IMPLEMENT QUEUE USING STACK (LEETCODE PROBLEM 232)
1) AIM:-Implement a first in first out (FIFO) queue using only two stacks. 
The implemented queue should support all the functions of a normal queue (push, peek, pop, and empty).

2) ALGORITH:-
Step 1: Initialize
     Create two empty stacks:
     s1 – stores the queue elements.
     s2 – used as a temporary stack during insertion.
Step 2: Push Operation (push(x))
     Move all elements from s1 to s2.
     Push the new element x into s1.
     Move all elements back from s2 to s1.
     Now, the front element of the queue remains at the top of s1.
Step 3: Pop Operation (pop())
     Store the top element of s1.
     Remove the top element from s1.
     Return the stored element.
Step 4: Peek Operation (peek())
    Return the top element of s1 without removing it.
Step 5: Empty Operation (empty())
    Check whether s1 is empty.
    If it is empty, return true; otherwise, return false.

3) CODE:-
class MyQueue {
public:
    MyQueue() {
        
    }
    stack<int> s1, s2;
    void push(int x) {
        while(!s1.empty()){
            s2.push(s1.top());
            s1.pop();
        }
        s1.push(x);
        while(!s2.empty()){
            s1.push(s2.top());
            s2.pop();
        }
    }
    
    int pop() {
        int store =s1.top();
        s1.pop();
        return store;
    }
    
    int peek() {
        return s1.top();
    }
    
    bool empty() {
        return s1.empty();
    }
};
